WEBVTT

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.460
Doing trick plays, letting him throw weak forkballs...

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.620
If I were his catcher, I would never let him do those kinds of things.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.810
Let's face him, Shigeno!

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:18.360
What!?

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.470
Don't run away, Shigeno!

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.710
That's not like you!

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.940
With just probabilities and petty tricks, we won't be able to defeat Kaido!

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.400
If there's any chance for us to win,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.090
it'll be with fastballs embedded with your spirit in a direct challenge!

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.910
<i>Bring it, Shigeno!</i>

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.740
Strike!

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.940
Batter out!

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.750
He did it!

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.320
All right!

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.040
<i>It's finally become an interesting game.</i>

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.800
<i>This was a miscalculation.</i>

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.570
<i>His pitching went up another level in speed, just by coming here...</i>

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.270
<i>and, moreover, why weren't any of them loose pitches?</i>

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:52.010
<i>Did my provocation bring out Goro-kun's hidden strength?</i>

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.310
Play!

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.360
Don't think your flukes and lucky plays will keep coming!

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.250
ALL RIGHT!

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.560
Were there any loose pitches back there?

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.060
No, none.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.550
Ever since Sato's last at-bat, not a single one.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.970
The game hasn't been progressing.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.900
Yeah.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.610
Seishuu tied it up,

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.070
but with the pitching change, their momentum has been halted.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.400
<i>Before he throws the knuckle ball, I have to get one of his pitches that increases the count...</i>

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:44.780
<i>and hit it!</i>

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.870
Out!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.520
It looks like Shigeno-kun's condition has gotten better,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.040
but they can't take the initiative from Kaido.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.230
Strike!

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.470
Batter out!

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:06.810
After this, the ultimate outcome depends on who takes the flow of the game.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:12.480
<i>If this inning ends with me, it'll be hard to score runs in the eighth and ninth innings.</i>

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.600
<i>If we don't get the lead before then...</i>

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:17.980
He hit it!

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.890
Out!

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.130
So close!

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.300
Didn't the wind blow that one back in!?

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.120
That was unlucky.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.130
So what?

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.710
We still have a chance.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:41.300
Even Kaido can't hit Shigeno's pitching right now.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.940
You guys have a good sense of giving the audience service.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.650
Thinking of ways to entertain the gallery with these developments...

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.200
But enough of that!

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.180
Come to your senses. This is preposterous!

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.440
Do you intend to lower the value of Kaido's brand?

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.540
Hurry up and finish them off!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.410
Strike!

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.920
<i>It's faster than before.</i>

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.500
<i>Anyway, I have to hit it, or else...</i>

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.330
Damn it!

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.590
It's going foul, Uchiyama!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.180
Safe!

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.950
S-Sorry.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.720
No worries.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.000
<i>Damn.</i>

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.310
<i>I was sure it'd be out.</i>

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:41.020
Batting ninth: pitcher, Akutsu-kun.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.360
<i>I won't let you go easily!</i>

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.410
Damn, that was a crappy bunt!

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:54.450
Safe!

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.230
Sorry.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.130
No worries.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.380
If I had just caught it...

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.210
No, it was my order in the first place...

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.410
Don't apologize.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:10.020
It's not like any of you are trying to mess up.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.850
Shigeno...

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.160
There's no need to worry. I won't let them hit.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.740
You guys helped me out earlier.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.720
It's time for me to pay back the favor.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.870
Batting first: center fielder, Kusano-kun.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.350
<i>If they take the lead and send out Mayumura, it'll be over for us!</i>

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.620
<i>I can't let them score a run here!</i>

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.600
<i>I can't expect to get loose pitches anymore.</i>

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:38.700
<i>I'll have to deal with whatever I get!</i>

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.130
<i>I ended up popping it up...</i>

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.010
All right, it's no outs and the bases are loaded!

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.630
They've finally started showing their true character.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:04.520
They were just lucky until now.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.740
<i>It's about time your bad-luck charm on us wore off.</i>

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.910
Batting second: second baseman, Tokashiki-kun.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.370
<i>Damn, is this it for us!?</i>

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.460
<i>We're just getting in Shigeno's way in the end!</i>

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.440
<i>Are we going to lose?</i>

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.570
<i>It's already the seventh inning.
They'll definitely use a squeeze!</i>

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.470
<i>For now, we'll go to the outside.</i>

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>That doesn't matter.</i>

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.510
<i>We're facing them, Tashiro!</i>

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:39.560
<i>What!?</i>

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.390
Strike!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.080
He doesn't seem to want to hold back at all.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.180
All right, call a squeeze next.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:04.780
<i>The first time I met Kaido face-to-face, you told me, Mayumura.</i>

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:09.610
<i>So what if they bunt? If you don't like it, don't let them do it.{M2-21 9:04}</i>

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:15.590
<i>If you don't have that confidence, then don't talk about having pride and being anti-manual. {M2-21 9:07.50}</i>

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:19.500
<i>I don't need the balls in the dirt or the forkball anymore.</i>

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.430
<i>I'll just trust in my pitches and bring you down!</i>

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.060
Foul!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.470
<i>How could I mess up a bunt?</i>

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:35.530
<i>I'll get it for sure this time!</i>

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.700
Strike!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.010
Batter out!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:47.550
Out!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.430
ALL RIGHT!

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.420
Two outs in one play!

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.510
Amazing, he shook off a bunt!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.340
Tokashiki!

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.930
You'll just stay on the bench after this inning!

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.320
I'm switching Kokubu in at second base!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:06.850
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:11.050
<i>If we aren't able to score a run when we have no outs and the bases loaded,</i>

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.460
<i>the flow will go back to Seishuu.</i>

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:20.410
<i>But a pitch that Tokashiki couldn't even make contact with...</i>

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:25.900
<i>Does Goro-kun still have a dormant power hidden in him?</i>

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.350
Batting third: third baseman, Yakushiji-kun.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:42.740
Two outs with a runner on second and third, and the third batter...

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.720
We can't relax yet.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.100
Strike!

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.340
<i>I'll acknowledge you, Shigeno.</i>

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:55.710
<i>In an environment you weren't satisfied with, to go to a low-level, third-class high school,</i>

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:58.570
<i>and still be able to push us this far...</i>

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.070
Foul!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:09.290
<i>That passion of yours to defeat Kaido was legit, huh?</i>

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.950
<i>However,</i>

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.250
<i>baseball is a sport you play with nine players.</i>

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:18.920
<i>With that pile of trash, you won't defeat us!</i>

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.310
Taiga, get it!

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.420
Out!

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.660
All right!

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:47.600
A-Amazing, he got it!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.500
Good going, Taiga!

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.520
Yonekura, come catch my pitches.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.330
I'm going to warm up just in case.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.890
Hey, wait a second.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:00.880
There's no need to!

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.830
You pitched first in the previous game.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.570
There's no plan for you to pitch today.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.250
"Plan"?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:13.020
Are you saying our manual planned for this kind of development?

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.640
Nice, Taiga!

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.690
We stopped them from scoring a run when they had the bases loaded!

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:23.310
What's wrong?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.410
Mayumura!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:33.040
I don't need Mayumura to cover for me!

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:37.250
Top of the eighth inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.170
Batting fourth: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.020
Strike!

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.060
Batter out!

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.140
Three outs! Change!

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.510
Another clean three up, three down.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:57.360
It's really turning out to be a one-run game.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.570
Just what I wanted!

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:04.720
Even with the flow from before,
Seishuu has a lot of pressure on them.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.120
Really? Isn't it still at Seishuu's pace?

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.790
They've always put their bet on winning a one-run game.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.170
That's true, but...

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.850
I wonder how much stamina Honda-kun has left.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.940
Bottom of the eighth inning: leading off for Kaido Academy...

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.720
Batting fourth: catcher, Sato-kun.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:31.640
In the game against us two weeks ago, he was only a relief pitcher.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.550
I don't think a foot injury that painful could have completely healed.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.240
Ball!

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.430
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:52.790
It couldn't have been easy getting this far either.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:58.440
Kaido still has Mayumura ready, so if this game goes into extra innings,

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:01.360
Seishuu doesn't have a chance to win then.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:04.780
Ball!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:05.720
Four balls!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.470
Hey, hey! What's wrong, Shigeno?

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.310
Is he trying to use the forkball again?

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.060
<i>That's strange.</i>

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:21.000
<i>All of a sudden, it looks like he's releasing the ball earlier in this inning.</i>

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.150
<i>A sacrifice bunt!?</i>

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:26.360
Like I'll let you!

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:29.780
All right!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.370
Huh?

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:43.410
This is a free fansub.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:43.410
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:48.430
Out!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.350
Out!

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.340
All right, a double play!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:54.470
Nice!

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.530
That guy...

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.730
Did he pretend to stagger in order to get them both out?

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.800
For him to pull a trick play like that...

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.440
Isn't that a little too easygoing?

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.780
<i>A trick play? That?</i>

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.440
That's not it.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:11.450
That was...

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.140
I see.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:23.950
I see now...

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:28.610
Izawa, call a bunt.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.930
Tell them to bunt.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.450
Bunt?

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.600
But we have two outs.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.900
Just shut up and give the sign.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.440
Safe!

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.350
There's no mistaking it!

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:05.000
With the injury in his right foot, he can't play at his best anymore!

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:06.960
Injury!?

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.620
<i>T-That's right!</i>

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:16.600
<i>I thought something was weird.
So the injury in Shigeno's right foot is...</i>

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.720
Get it, Yaoita?

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.600
It's only a matter of time!

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.580
Break him down thoroughly and send him to Hell!

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:31.150
Y-Yes.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.800
The injury from back when he went against our second team?

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.100
He hasn't recovered from that yet?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:40.750
How can he pitch like he has under those conditions?

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:47.590
He was likely depending on painkillers, but those have a limit too.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:53.300
If they didn't, there wouldn't have been a reason to arrange a game with the second team.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.100
"Arrange"?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.340
What do you mean, Egashira-san?

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.350
He turned his back on Kaido.

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:05.700
If we had someone like him continuing in baseball on a grand scale, it'd be displeasing, wouldn't it?

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:11.750
Shigeno-kun still hasn't recovered from that injury after all...

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:16.990
It can't be...

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.080
You had a game against him in order to injure him?

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.790
Don't make me out to be the bad guy.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:27.130
<i>P-Please stop the jokes!</i>

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.880
<i>I can't do that...</i>

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:31.420
<i>Is that so?</i>

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.350
<i>It's all right if you don't want to.</i>

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:37.050
<i>I'll just use another player who wants to be promoted to the first team.</i>

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:40.590
<i>That's too bad, Kamata-kun.</i>

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:47.970
<i>You finally pulled through Dream Island, but you'll just be in the stands cheering for the others in the end.</i>

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:07.290
He can protest however he likes, but there's no proof.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.460
You don't have to worry about anything. Just crush him completely!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.840
Strike!

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:19.960
Is that so?

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:23.700
Just because my foot seems to hurt a little, you pester me with bunting.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:27.100
It sounds just like something that stingy daddy's boy would think of.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.580
But, you see,

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.340
unfortunately for you, my foot doesn't hurt at all!

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.320
I still have plenty of stamina too!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.780
I can run through tens of more innings,

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:41.620
and I can keep pitching through tens and hundreds of pitches like this!

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.720
I won't lose!

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:47.710
I'll keep going until things come our way and it's game over!

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.750
What an obvious bluff!

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.720
Don't hold back!

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.980
Until he's screaming in agony and cowering on the mound,

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.320
thoroughly break him by bunting!

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:04.600
Ball!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.100
Ball two!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:14.890
What? He's still throwing with all he's got.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:18.380
Doesn't that mean that foot injury isn't doing much?

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.170
That'd be good if it were true.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:26.180
But it's just like Honda-kun to pretend like it isn't doing much and be reckless.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.540
You know that too, don't you, Shimizu-san?

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.410
U-Uh, yeah.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.880
<i>Yeah. Yeah, but...</i>

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.770
<i>I don't want to believe it.</i>

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.270
Ball!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.390
Ball three!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.310
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.510
<i>And we knew it all along!</i>

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:05.740
<i>His right foot isn't completely healed at all!</i>

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>Yet he, without ever complaining to us,</i>

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.540
<i>has been throwing, hitting, running...</i>

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.880
<i>He's been playing baseball all of his own accord!</i>

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.420
Miyazaki!

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.630
Uchiyama!

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:25.200
Get closer and help Shigeno out!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.620
We won't let them do us in with a strategy like this!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.220
<i>That's right, this time we'll be...</i>

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:35.810
<i>the ones to help Shigeno out!</i>

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.240
T-Tashiro!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:51.790
Out!

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.410
Three outs! Change!

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:58.630
Can none of these guys even bunt properly!?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.230
Change! Hurry and bring him down!

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:07.430
Got it!? It's the ninth inning now!

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:11.860
With Shigeno's condition, we can't go into extra innings!

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:14.440
We have to finish things off this inning!

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.050
Hey, come on.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.280
Who can't fight in extra innings?

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.490
If you're talking about me-

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:20.350
Shut your hole!

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:21.900
Injured people should stay quiet!

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:26.240
We can't let it end like this!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:32.910
Do whatever you can to get in the ring and win before they take down Shigeno!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:34.890
Yeah!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:38.520
Strike!

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.700
Batter out!

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.030
Strike!

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.300
Batter out!

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:48.300
Batting ninth: left fielder, Noguchi-kun.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.630
<i>Goro-kun's strength greatly surpassed my calculations.</i>

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:58.270
<i>If he didn't have his foot injury,
he might have cornered us even further.</i>

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:04.180
<i>If what Egashira-san said is true,
and we were to win because of that...</i>

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.110
Sato!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:16.670
Safe!

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:18.050
All right!

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.250
We have a runner!

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.510
S-Sorry.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.960
Oh well.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.420
So, he's next...

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:30.180
If things are looking bad, it'll be okay if we walk him.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.600
Anyway, don't throw any weak pitches!

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:36.130
Akutsu is going to hit 50 pitches soon.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:37.600
We usually bench him around then.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.900
I know that already!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:41.700
But they already have two outs.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.490
We'll replace Akutsu when he goes to bat this inning.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:50.870
If we can end it like that, we won't have to send out Mayumura.

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>Seishuu baseball club?</i>

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:05.180
<i>Are you kidding?</i>

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:08.630
<i>What can a new baseball club do?</i>

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:11.540
<i>If you think I'm tricking you,
why don't you just check them out?</i>

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:14.890
<i>There's a really outrageous guy with them.</i>

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:18.970
<i>He intends to take down Kaido by himself!</i>

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:21.150
<i>What's that?</i>

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:22.700
<i>That's laughable.</i>

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:26.150
Hit, Taiga!

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:36.990
<i>Let me be safe!</i>

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:38.710
<i>I have to be safe!</i>

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:47.670
Safe! Safe!

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:49.630
They did it!

00:22:50.150 --> 00:22:51.020
Nice one!

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:52.590
That was awesome!

00:24:40.540 --> 00:24:44.170
Toshiya directly confronts Egashira and his methods.

00:24:44.170 --> 00:24:48.170
To counter him, Egashira threatens to expel Toshiya from the baseball club.

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:51.880
Pride or victory, what will Kaido choose?

00:24:52.730 --> 00:24:54.130
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.130 --> 00:24:55.940
The End of the Artifice.

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:58.190
Run to the stage of your dreams!
